Upstream-bound: no
Subject: [PORT_HOST] P6.1 area-change iris and grid cover reach the 16:9 picture

FIELDSTG_closeField shrinks the map's clip rectangle (a 320 x 240 box that
starts at the whole screen and centres on the player) and then closes the blue
grid cover from both sides. A drawing area only takes the side gutters when it
spans the display's columns, so the box and the closing grid were 4:3 with
black gutters (0051 only widened the cover's blocks).

With widescreen on (gutter > 0; off, the code is the PS1's):
- substate 1: the map layer keeps a display-wide area, clipped in rows only
  (it takes the gutters), and the view closes from 320 + 2 * gutter columns, the
  game's own task->width scaled, so the frame count does not change. The columns
  outside the view get the grid over black, drawn in the map layer by the new
  FIELDSTG_drawCoverSpan (a copy of FIELDSTG_drawCoverBlock cropped to a column
  range, with an opaque black quad under it), so the map no longer shows there.
- substate 2: the cover layer keeps a display-wide area and the grid closes
  from the edges of the gutters to the middle in the same 20 steps; the map
  layer's area is moved to a row below the display, which draws nothing. That
  also avoids the PC sdl3_gpu bug of a 0x0 clip keeping the previous scissor (the
  shifted map that showed again while the grid closed) for this path.

